{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-159946",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the log-likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡L(\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta )) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{i};\\theta )).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=12$ independent normal random variables with unknown mean $\\theta $ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=1,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x,\\theta )=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{e}^{-(x-\\theta )^{2}/2},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nNext, we write down the log-density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡f(x,\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi }}{e}^{-(x-\\theta )^{2}/2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi }})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-(x-\\theta )^{2}/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{(x-\\theta )^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can calculate the log-likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{({x}_{i}-\\theta )^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{n}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{({x}_{i}-\\theta )^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-2\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}+n{\\theta }^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=40,$ ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2}=150.86,$ and $n=12.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =-\\frac{12}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}(150.86-2\\theta \\cdot 40+12{\\theta }^{2}) \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2\\pi )+(-75.43)+40\\theta +(-6){\\theta }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=(-75.43)+40+(-6)=-41.43.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
